# TI-EP-005 — Commentary Persistence Layer

**Project:** BTA V5 — HCGO Commentary / Scholars Persistence

**Status:** Locked — July 2026

**Classification:** Technical Implementation — Persistence

---

## Section 1 — Purpose

Defines the persistence structure for downloaded commentary content
(currently: CCEL-sourced public domain commentary — Matthew Henry,
John Wesley, Charles Spurgeon, Adam Clarke, Albert Barnes).

This is the content layer TI-EP-001 named but never instantiated
(`Expert Identity -> referenced_by -> Commentary`). `expert_identity`
stores WHO a commentator is; this table stores WHAT they wrote.

Greenfield build — no migration/backfill required.

Scripture verse text itself (the primary source text) remains on the
existing Bible API path and is explicitly out of scope for this
document — only scholarly commentary content is brought into
Postgres, because that is the content the API cannot decompose to
the granularity BTA needs.

---

## Section 2 — Table Definition

```sql
CREATE TABLE commentary (
    commentary_id   UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),

    -- who wrote it
    expert_id       UUID NOT NULL,

    -- domain isolation (same pattern as expert_identity)
    domain_id       UUID NOT NULL,

    -- passage reference
    book            TEXT NOT NULL,
    chapter         INT  NOT NULL,
    verse_start     INT  NOT NULL,
    verse_end       INT  NOT NULL,

    -- content
    body_text       TEXT NOT NULL,

    -- provenance / licensing
    ingestion_source TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'CCEL',
    source_edition   TEXT,
    license_status   TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'PUBLIC_DOMAIN',

    -- lifecycle / governance metadata (per PA-EP-001 principle 12)
    status          TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'DRAFT',
    reviewed_by     UUID,
    reviewed_at     TIMESTAMP,

    created_at      TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at      TIMESTAMP DEFAULT now(),

    CONSTRAINT fk_commentary_expert
        FOREIGN KEY (expert_id)
        REFERENCES expert_identity(expert_id)
        ON DELETE RESTRICT,

    CONSTRAINT fk_commentary_domain
        FOREIGN KEY (domain_id)
        REFERENCES domain(domain_id)
        ON DELETE RESTRICT,

    CONSTRAINT verse_range_valid
        CHECK (verse_end >= verse_start),

    CONSTRAINT license_status_valid
        CHECK (license_status IN ('PUBLIC_DOMAIN','LICENSED','RESTRICTED')),

    CONSTRAINT commentary_status_valid
        CHECK (status IN ('DRAFT','PUBLISHED','ARCHIVED'))
);
```

