## Section 5 — Design Decisions (Resolved July 2026)

**1. Passage reference format — LOCKED.**
`book` / `chapter` / `verse_start` / `verse_end` is confirmed as the
canonical, enterprise-wide scripture reference standard for BTA V5
Commentary — not commentary-specific, not temporary. Matches existing
BTA retrieval logic and Bible API reference resolution. OSHA
intentionally uses a separate citation hierarchy (standard/section);
that separation is correct and stays as-is.

**2. Expert/type relationship — LOCKED.**
Only `expert_identity` rows with `type = 'commentary_source'` may
have associated `commentary` rows. Enforced via trigger (Section 4.1)
— Postgres CHECK constraints cannot query another table, so this
could not be done via CHECK as originally proposed. Prevents OSHA
entities, CRM contacts, or future-domain actors from incorrectly
generating commentary content.

**3. Write-logging trigger — LOCKED (implementation fix applied).**
`log_domain_write_attempt()` now uses `TG_TABLE_NAME` instead of a
hardcoded `entity_type` value (Section 4.2). This was a required
correction, not optional — the original TI-EP-003 version would have
mislabeled every `commentary` write as an `expert_identity` write.

**4. Multi-edition / duplicate handling — LOCKED (no UNIQUE constraint).**
Duplicates are allowed by design — CCEL or future sources may
legitimately provide multiple editions of the same commentator's work
on the same passage, and forcing uniqueness would break ingestion
flexibility. Resolution of which edition displays happens at the
application/retrieval layer, not the database layer.

**Open follow-up (not a lock blocker):** the intended retrieval rule
references a `trust_level` concept ("resolve via ingestion_source
priority rules") that does not yet exist as a column anywhere in the
schema — not on `commentary`, `expert_identity`, or any
`ingestion_source` table. This needs to be defined (which table it
lives on, what values it takes) before the retrieval-layer resolution
logic can actually be built. Tracked as an open item for the next
ingestion-layer design pass, not required before this table locks.

**5. Section 6 scope — CONFIRMED UNCHANGED.**
`bible_reference_index` (verse caching) remains deferred. OSHA content
remains a separate domain/table structure. Orchestration, Memory, and
Commercial layers are not part of this document. Later mapping-
foundation documents proposing broader scope do not override this.

